            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Punjabi for a guess, then the Punjabi for to seem right."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ਸਮਝਾਉਣਾ",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ਸਮਝਾਉਣਾ — samjhāuṇā — \"to explain\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ਕੀ ਅਧਿਆਪਕ ਹਰ ਸਵਾਲ ਸਮਝਾਉਂਦਾ ਹੈ? kī adhiāpak har savāl samjhāundā hai? Does the teacher explain every question?"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past (I …): ਮੈਂ ਸਵਾਲ ਸਮਝਾਇਆ, maiṁ savāl samjhāiā."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ਸਮਝਾਉਣਾ (samjhāuṇā) is the causative partner of samajhṇā, \"to understand\", which goes back to Sanskrit saṁbudhyate, \"wakes up, understands\"; CDIAL lists Punjabi samajhṇā under it (CDIAL 12959)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for asking and answering."
